+//! End-to-end: the ported verifier sub-circuit verifies real SHA-384/Ext12 child proofs.
+//!
+//!   cargo test --release -p openvm-recursion-circuit --lib e2e_ -- --nocapture
+//!
+//! **Legacy (2026-10-21).** These tests exercise `system::VerifierSubCircuit`, which the `nv`
+//! circuit replaced; `nv` builds from `transcript2::replay2` and never touches `system`. The
+//! circuit here replays its transcript with `sha_transcript::replay_transcript`, whose squeeze is
+//! the old chained `H(5, sigma_j)`. T\* (final-soundness G-1/G-2) changed the deployed transcript
+//! to counter mode `H(5, kappa || le32(j))` and updated `nv`'s `replay2` but not this path, so
+//! the replay now disagrees with the recorded samples and the three tests below panic at
+//! `sha_transcript.rs` "transcript replay disagrees with recorded sample". That is a stale
+//! debug path, not a soundness bug: no gate runs these, and the live NV suite (`nv::`) is green.
+//! They are `#[ignore]`d rather than deleted so the code stays compilable and greppable; port
+//! them to `replay2` only if `system::VerifierSubCircuit` is ever revived.
